// # Sec Submodule Hub -- Zero-Drag
//
// Logline: Unified entry point for the standard sec (security) domain library. Re-exports a stable sec_mod_* surface for the most-used public API (capability rights, host scope, path scope, fuel budget, tamper shield, watermark, redteam vectors, attestation, safety matrix, fuzz runner, mutation engine, rlimit). Private siblings (Bell-LaPadula, Biba, Clark-Wilson, Dolev-Yao, capability unforgeability, fail-secure, Kerckhoffs, least privilege, non-interference, provable security, sel4 isolation, TLS 1.3 handshake, zero trust, AC theory) remain non-public in sec/laws/.
//
// Setup: Imports private sec siblings; most operations take SysCap / FsReadCap / FsWriteCap / EnvCap at the call site. Pure security math (capability rights, host scope, path scope, tamper shield, watermark) takes no caps.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Re-export the capability-rights and host/path scope surface as sec_mod_cap_*, sec_mod_host_*, sec_mod_path_*.
//   2. Re-export the tamper shield, watermark, and fuel budget surface as sec_mod_tamper_*, sec_mod_watermark_*, sec_mod_fuel_*.
//   3. Re-export the agent send, redteam vectors, and policy path surface as sec_mod_msg_*, sec_mod_redteam_*, sec_mod_policy_*.
//   4. Re-export the safety matrix, fuzz runner, mutation engine, attestation, TEE quote, and rlimit surface as sec_mod_safety_*, sec_mod_fuzz_*, sec_mod_mutation_*, sec_mod_attest_*, sec_mod_tee_*, sec_mod_rlimit_*.
//   5. Re-export the new subdirs: sec/hash/, sec/simd/, sec/symmetric/, sec/asymmetric/, sec/mac/, sec/zk/, sec/enclave/, sec/laws/.
//   6. Document the private siblings that external callers must NOT import directly: _law, _theory, _principle, _invariants, _kat, _stubs files.

